{
  "title": "Extract mana handling from BridgeCallbackHandler.java",
  "description": "The bridge refactor pulled out read-only helpers, but mana payment is still concentrated in `BridgeCallbackHandler.java`. `handleGamePlayManaAuto()` starts around line 4926, with supporting helpers such as `getPoolManaChoices()`, `parseManaPlan()`, `cancelSpellFromBadManaPlan()`, and the pool-loop detection logic nearby.\n\nThat code currently owns several distinct behaviors at once:\n- parsing and consuming model-provided mana plans\n- inspecting mana pools and picking deterministic pool-mana options\n- ordering auto-tap candidates from `canPlayObjects`\n- loop detection and cancellation semantics for failed payment progress\n- MCP-vs-auto runtime branching for manual pool choice fallthrough\n\nSuggested split:\n1. `ManaPlanParser` / `ManaPlanState` for the plan representation\n2. `ManaHandler` for auto-pay execution and cancellation rules\n3. focused tests for pool-loop cancellation, exhausted plans, bad short IDs, and deterministic source ordering\n\nThis is still one of the highest-risk areas in the bridge because it mutates live payment state and has to stay deterministic under retries.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "bridge",
    "refactoring",
  ],
